# Building runs the initializer, and an initializer another one calls (`super().__init__()`) builds nothing: it fills in
# the value its caller builds. So each build is the value it makes and nothing else: `Expert(2)` takes no Expert, though
# one was built just before it, and the mixture takes the two experts it is handed. Each base initializer prints.

route experts.run
step run/Expert()
step run/Expert()/Component()
step run/Expert()#2
step run/Expert()#2/Component()
step run/Mixture()
step run/Mixture()/Component()

line entry > run call
line run/Expert()/Component() > Screen own
line run/Expert()#2/Component() > Screen own
line run/Mixture()/Component() > Screen own
line run/Expert() > Expert·small@run/Expert() value
line run/Expert()#2 > Expert·large@run/Expert()#2 value
line Expert·small@run/Expert() > run/Mixture() value          # the mixture reads the size of each expert it is handed
line Expert·large@run/Expert()#2 > run/Mixture() value
line run/Mixture() > Mixture·mixture@run/Mixture() value
line Mixture·mixture@run/Mixture() > run value                # run prints a field of the mixture it built
line run > Screen own

home Expert·small@run/Expert() run
home Expert·large@run/Expert()#2 run
home Mixture·mixture@run/Mixture() run

side entry left
side Screen right
